  "name": "API key masking in provider table",
  "pinned": false,
  "description": "# Conversation Summary\n\n1. **Requested Change**: Modified the API Key display in the AIProviders table to show a masked format instead of just the first 4 characters and dots.\n\n2. **Implementation**: Added a new `maskApiKey()` method to the component that displays the first 6 characters and last 5 characters of the API key, with bullet points (\u2022) masking the middle portion.\n\n3. **Use Case**: This provides better visual identification of API keys for users to verify they're viewing the correct key without exposing sensitive data.\n\n4. **Code Update**: Replaced the simple slice operation in the template with a call to the new `maskApiKey()` method for improved security and usability.\n\n5. **Result**: Users can now quickly verify API keys by seeing the beginning and end characters (e.g., `sk-123\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u20221234567890`) while keeping the middle section hidden.",
